# What a reuse of a pane slot does to every field of `Pane` and `Vt` (tests/vt/reuse_fields.py holds it).
# A slot is never dropped: the next pane takes the first free slot (acquire_pane, which calls fresh_screen, which
# calls vt.reuse), and spawn_pane_in and start_pane give it its new identity and program.
#   STRUCT FIELD reset CHAIN      reset at the end of CHAIN (f1>f2>...: f1 calls f2 ..., the last names .FIELD)
#   STRUCT FIELD kept -- WHY      keeps its value, rightly
#   STRUCT FIELD counter -- WHY   only grows, and nothing reads it as the last program's
# A full reset (RIS) is reached from vt.reuse by the bytes it feeds, through the parser to `ESC c`.
alias ris reuse>feed>feed_byte>dispatch_grid_token>dispatch_escape>full_reset

Pane live reset spawn_pane_in
Pane id reset spawn_pane_in
Pane session reset spawn_pane_in
Pane session_gen reset spawn_pane_in
Pane gen reset spawn_pane_in
Pane master reset spawn_pane_in>start_pane
Pane key reset spawn_pane_in
Pane child reset spawn_pane_in>start_pane
Pane pid reset spawn_pane_in>start_pane
Pane child_live reset spawn_pane_in>start_pane
Pane status reset spawn_pane_in>start_pane
Pane ended reset spawn_pane_in>start_pane
Pane screen reset acquire_pane>fresh_screen
Pane input kept -- contents only: nothing reads past in_len, which start_pane resets
Pane in_off reset spawn_pane_in>start_pane
Pane in_len reset spawn_pane_in>start_pane
Pane write_on reset spawn_pane_in>start_pane
Pane last_output reset spawn_pane_in
Pane sync_since reset acquire_pane>fresh_screen
Pane read_turn counter -- the turn of the last read: the frame reads it only to count prompt frames, a trace statistic, and the new program's first read sets it
Pane streaming reset spawn_pane_in>start_pane
Pane read_peak reset spawn_pane_in>start_pane
Pane damage reset spawn_pane_in
Pane shown reset spawn_pane_in
Pane at_col kept -- set when the pane is laid out shown (sync_sizes), and read only while shown, which spawn_pane_in clears
Pane at_row kept -- set when the pane is laid out shown (sync_sizes), and read only while shown, which spawn_pane_in clears
Pane argv reset spawn_pane_in
Pane start_dir reset spawn_pane_in

Vt cols reset reuse>resize
Vt rows reset reuse>resize
Vt primary reset @ris
Vt alternate reset @ris
Vt active_alternate reset @ris>alternate_state
Vt cursor_row reset @ris
Vt cursor_col reset @ris
Vt cursor_shape reset @ris
Vt pending_wrap reset @ris>soft_reset
Vt region_top reset @ris>soft_reset
Vt region_bottom reset @ris>soft_reset
Vt tabs reset @ris
Vt default_tabs reset @ris
Vt pen reset @ris>soft_reset>reset_pen
Vt modes reset @ris
Vt parser reset @ris
Vt title_storage kept -- contents only: nothing reads past title_length
Vt title_length reset reuse>forget_title
Vt cwd_storage kept -- contents only: nothing reads past cwd_length
Vt cwd_length reset reuse>forget_reported_dir
Vt local_host reset spawn_pane_in>set_local_host
Vt local_host_length reset spawn_pane_in>set_local_host
Vt mode_values reset @ris>change_mode_value
Vt events reset reuse>take_events
Vt scrollback_cap_bytes kept -- the server's one history cap, the same for every pane
Vt answer_storage kept -- contents only: nothing reads past answer_length
Vt answer_length reset @ris
Vt saved_primary reset @ris
Vt saved_alternate reset @ris
Vt g0 reset @ris
Vt g1 reset @ris
Vt shifted reset @ris
Vt last_printed reset @ris
Vt last_mark1 reset @ris
Vt last_mark2 reset @ris
Vt combine_row reset @ris>clear_combine_anchor
Vt combine_col reset @ris>clear_combine_anchor
Vt wide_run reset reuse>feed>feed_byte
Vt history reset @ris
Vt line_coordinate reset @ris
Vt resize_state reset reuse>feed
Vt glyph_calls counter -- the scalars the per-glyph path wrote, read only by rows
Vt tick counter -- damage ticks only grow, so a reused pane's cells are new to every client
